>
> The key point is that we have tons of people DISCUSSING ABOUT the language 
> and very few people actually USING it.
>

Sure. But having dispersed material doesn't help newcomers.
 

> The only way, to me, to make the language evolve is to actually doing 
> something with it. The key points, imho, that make Lojban and should never 
> be abandonded are:
>
>  - Statement as relation (as opposed to Subject/Verb/objects)
>  - Formal grammar to resolve any parsing ambiguity (I really welcomed 
> moving to PEG).
>

Looks like a very shortened "Lojban fundamentals" I was trying to achieve! 
Thanks. I'll note that.

